                <a href="/projects/guide-ceh-p-master.mirror/" title="Find out more about Guide-CEH-Practical-Master" class="summary-inline">Guide CEH Practical Master is a study and reference repository for the Certified Ethical Hacker Practical examination. It documents the exam format, practical challenge structure, environment, and general preparation considerations. The guide covers network scanning, enumeration, vulnerability analysis, system security, cryptography, packet analysis, web vulnerabilities, and digital forensics. It collects references for widely used security tools such as Nmap, Wireshark, Metasploit, Hashcat, and SQLmap. Practice resources include labs, vulnerable machines, challenge platforms, cheat sheets, and external tutorials. The repository also provides example question styles and extensive links organized around common ethical hacking topics.</a>
            
